 "notes_text": "Shadow. A pedal 'u' on Eb5 under two falling sighs (Eb | G-F, then Eb | Ab-G) over a tonic pedal that rocks i <-> VI6, where only G<->Ab moves in the chord: the same semitone the melody sighs on, so the rocking is quieter and more hypnotic than the original's diminished pendulum. Spins: a turn on the pedal note (bar 4), an upper-neighbour turn (bar 5) and a chromatic lift F#-G-A (bar 6) into the cry: Bb5 over a 'Hungarian' V7/V (D7 with b13) at 7.9 s, falling a semitone to A5, the darkest and most Eastern-European colour of the four and a different cry note from the original's Ab. After a lower-neighbour turn over V7, the cadence gives one last Ab->G sigh as V7 arrives, then a falling triplet F-D into the tonic a triplet early, held over the waltz, with V7(b9) under it at the end for the loop. Range C5-Bb5 (a minor 7th), 95 % of the notes inside a fifth."
